🌿 Environmental Measurement vs. Estimation Categorization
To maintain complete academic rigor, environmental variables are categorized into direct telemetry measurements vs. calculated physics estimates:



┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      ENVIRONMENTAL VARIABLE CLASSIFICATION ARCHITECTURE                   │
├───────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🛰️ DIRECTLY MEASURED TELEMETRY             │ 🧮 CALCULATED / ESTIMATED INDICATORS          │
├───────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ • Queue Staging Delay (Hours)             │ • Reefer Fuel Burn Avoided (Liters)          │
│ • Axle Weights & Gross Mass (WIM Scales)  │   (T_saved × 2.50 L/hr)                       │
│ • License Plate & ISO Code (OCR Cameras)  │ • Net CO₂ Emissions Avoided (kg CO₂)          │
│ • Manifest Hash Validation (RFID Scans)   │   (Liters Saved × 2.68 kg CO₂/L)              │
│ • Sub-500ms Decision Latency (Node.js)    │ • Scope 3 ESG Monetary Value (€ Saved)        │
└───────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────┘


Measured Telemetry Parameters (Phase 1): Edge sensors directly capture physical vehicle attributes (gross mass, axle count, timestamp, plate ID) and queue waiting times at the Dorohusk checkpoint.
Estimated Environmental Indicators (Phase 1): Avoided auxiliary diesel burn and net $\text{CO}_2$ reductions are calculated by running measured time-savings through verified physics constants (Thermo King 2.50 L/hr fuel burn rate and EEA 2.68 kg $\text{CO}_2$/L emission factor).
🧭 Phase 1 Scope vs. Phase 2 Field Validation Requirements
🏛️ Phase 1: Immediate Scope & Deliverables (VCBIP 2026 Window)
Conceptual Digital Twin & Shadow Engine: Deploying the sub-500ms 3-Gate decision engine in a passive shadow sandbox (sandbox/server.js) to process duplicated telemetry without disrupting live border operations.
SCADA Control Viewport: Providing border control officers with a WebGL Digital Twin interface displaying real-time pass/fail clearance flags and live sustainability metrics.
Fixed B2G Financial Architecture: Relying exclusively on fixed enterprise B2G revenue (R.1 Setup Fees €15k–€30k, R.2 Annual SaaS €25k–€60k, and R.3 Remote Governance €5k–€7.5k) during the initial 24-month validation window. Zero dependence on speculative carbon offset sales or volumetric fees.
🚀 Phase 2: Deferred Strategic Vision & Field Validation (Years 3+)
Live IoT Fuel Telemetry Audits: Replacing estimated reefer fuel burn (2.50 L/hr) with direct CAN-bus/IoT fuel tank sensors across participating 3PL carrier fleets to establish certified MRV carbon accounting.
Volumetric Commercial Scaling: Unlocking volumetric transaction micro-billing (R.4), B2B Scope 3 audit fees (R.5), and certified carbon credit trading (R.6) after regulatory MRV verification.
Heavy Physical Civil Expansions: Physical rail line construction, automated shuttle conveyors, microgrid (BESS) peak-shaving hardware, and $\text{CaCO}_3$ circularity loops remain isolated under /legacy/ as future strategic expansion options.
